  <data name="Category_articles_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use a/an with a singular countable noun the first time you mention it, and the for something known or already mentioned. Don't put the before general nouns: Life is short, not The life is short.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.articles.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_prepositions_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Prepositions often don't translate word for word: in for months, years and cities; on for days and dates; at for times and exact places. Some verbs take no preposition: discuss the plan, not discuss about the plan.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.prepositions.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_verb_tense_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use the past simple for something finished at a known time (I finished yesterday), and the present perfect for something with an effect now or no set time (I have finished). Don't use the continuous with state verbs: I know, not I am knowing.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.verb_tense.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_agreement_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>With he / she / it or a singular noun, the present-tense verb takes s: She works, The team is. With plurals it doesn't: They work, The results are.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.agreement.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_plurals_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use the plural after numbers and words like many / several / one of the: three days, one of the best places. Some nouns have no plural: information, advice, equipment.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.plurals.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_word_choice_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Literal translations give words that are correct but unnatural. Learn common combinations as a whole: make a decision, not do a decision; take a photo, not make a photo.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.word_choice.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_spelling_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Watch words that sound alike: their / there / they're, your / you're, its / it's.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.spelling.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_punctuation_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start sentences, names, days, months and I with a capital letter. Put a space after commas and full stops, not before them.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.punctuation.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_word_order_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Adjectives come before the noun (a big house), and indirect questions use statement order: Can you tell me where the station is, not where is the station.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.word_order.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Category_sentence_structure_Tip" xml:space="preserve"><value>English sentences are shorter than Arabic ones. Don't join two full sentences with just a comma; use a full stop or and / but / so / because.</value><comment>CATEGORIES.sentence_structure.tip</comment></data>
  <data name="Journal_Summary" xml:space="preserve"><value>You proofread {0} and {1} found.{2} Click a type to see its rule and examples from your writing.</value><comment>o.jSummary, a function in Lamha 2 (Arabic counting), ported by hand: {0} the texts, {1} the mistakes, {2} Journal_Top or nothing</comment></data>
