  <data name="Settings_PrivacyText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sent to Google&apos;s translation service: the text you select, and the sentence around it (if “Understand words from their sentence” is on). The word is sent to Wikipedia for the summary. In “Offline only” mode, words are looked up without sending anything. For a price in your currency, the day&apos;s exchange rates are fetched, without anything you selected. With the writing tools, the text goes to the provider you chose: Gemini, Claude or OpenAI with your key, or the server you set up; with Ollama or a server on your PC it stays on your computer. Clipboard history stays on this PC. No other data is collected.</value><comment>o.privacyText reworded 2026-10-25 (approved: &quot;go with your recommendation&quot;): the app, not a browser; the five providers, prices and clipboard history</comment></data>
